"""Writes what today's Python computes for the Google connectors' TypeScript port.

Tables (generated source, committed):
- src/lib/zones.ts: the IANA time zone names Python's zoneinfo offers.

Vectors (test/fixtures/connectors/google/): vectors.json for Calendar and Drive (input validation, dates and
times), and gmail.json for Gmail (input validation, MIME parsing and building, header decoding, address
headers, base64, which charset labels Python knows, mail addresses and the HTML converter), as backend/connectors/ computes them.

The digit ranges of src/lib/digits.ts are checked against Python (`check_digits`). Case folding and lowercasing
come from the runtime (src/lib/casefold.ts, lower.ts) and are checked against Python 3.14 for every code point
by test/fixtures/unicode/generate.py.

Only connector modules are imported (they load no configuration). Run from cloudflare/:
cd ../backend && .venv/bin/python -I ../cloudflare/test/fixtures/connectors/google/generate.py

The committed vectors keep a sample of each random group (ISO_RANDOM, ISO_DATES, BASE64_RANDOM,
ADDRESSES_RANDOM, HTML_RANDOM, RAW_RANDOM) to stay under about 500 KB per file; add `--full` (after the
script's path) for the whole set, about 1.9 MB together, for a local run. The tables above do not depend on it.
"""

